// Evergrove's Mimic minigame recipes: Cooking now, later Smelting, Sword and Music. SOE's MimicMiniGameData.txt and
// MimicMiniGamePhaseData.txt never shipped with the client, so every recipe and number here is ours. The fields are
// explained in src/Sanctuary.Game/Minigames/Mimic/MimicDefinition.cs and docs/research/mimic.md.
//
// A recipe is a Games menu entry (ActivityId, the client's ClientActivityDefinitions row) played as rounds, one per
// phase. Each phase becomes one row of MimicMiniGamePhaseData.txt; Data is LD_DATA1 onward, missing columns are sent as
// 0. GameId is the recipe's own Mimic game id (any number but 47, which shows Cooking's promotion banner).
//
// Cooking's rounds (StageType) and what their Data columns mean; Data[0] is always the ingredient, and the server
// refuses one the round's scene has no picture for (Sanctuary.Game/Minigames/Mimic/CookingStages.cs):
//   1 tenderize   [meat, hits needed 1-30, start speed, acceleration 1-100, top speed 25-100, hits per smash 1-10,
//                  points per hit, hammer size +0-300%]                          meat: 8 mystery, 9 bear, 10 bat, 11 spider
//   2 chop        [leaf, chops 1-20, clicks per chop 1-5, slices per chop 1-10, points per slice]
//                                                     leaf: 24 rainleaf, 25 sunleaf, 26 spiralmint, 27 scragglevine, 28 florenleaf
//   3 smashFruit  [fruit, hits per fruit 1-15, fruits 1-6, hammer size, meter speed medium, high (10-100), hits for a
//                  good and a perfect smash, points weak, good, perfect]       fruit: 34-41, 56 tomato (40 gummyfruit)
//   4 crack       [23 egg, cracks per egg, eggs 1-5, points per egg, hammer size, meter speed medium, high]
//   6 measure     [liquid, good within 5-50, perfect within, points good, perfect]
//                                                     liquid: 19 slugmud, 20 rootbeer, 48-53 broths, 21/22 ice, 23 egg
//   7 stir        [46 meat stew / 47 fish soup / 54 spaghetti, turns 1-50, % chance to switch direction, points per
//                  turn, bonus per correct turn]      needs an earlier measure round: its liquid is the broth
//   9 grate       [31 chugaroot / 32 chocolate / 33 honeytwig, swipes 3-15, bowl's sway seconds 1-15, sway distance
//                  0-480, points, feedback every N (0 = 5)]
//  10 slice       [vegetable, cuts, -, good cut within px, perfect within px, points bad, good, perfect, pieces per
//                  perfect 1-5]                       vegetable: 12-18, 57 onion (12 tumtumnip, 13 moonbean, 14 choychoy)
//  11 cook        [42 meat saute / 43 fish saute / 54 spaghetti]  the other columns 0 keeps the Flash's own heat table
//  12 cut         [fish 0-7, points good, perfect]
//  13 setHeat     [21 vanilla / 22 chocolate ice, -, points]
//  17 addIngredients [42 meat saute, 43 fish saute, 44 sundae, 45 omelet, 46 meat stew, 47 fish soup, 54 spaghetti;
//                  1 = list in the order gathered, else reversed; points per ingredient (500 or more)]
// The add-ingredients and cook rounds use what the tenderize, chop, smash, grate, slice and cut rounds before them
// gathered. There is no pour scene in this Flash.
//
// Coins and Experience (Chef stars) are paid for a win and are placeholders until the economy pass.
